# Generalize similar UI/UX fixes

When resolving a **user-visible** UI or UX defect, do not stop at the first widget that showed the bug. Search for the same pattern elsewhere and fix those sites in the **same turn** when the same user would hit them.

## Do

- After the local fix is clear, scan for the same cause (same layout quirk, missing enable rule, icon/height/scroll behavior, menu/action gap).
- Prefer one shared helper over copying the same workaround into each view.
- Cover every list, pane, or dialog where the defect can actually appear.

## Skip

- Sites that cannot show the problem (no icons, one column, already handled).
- Unrelated polish, refactors, or extras that are not this defect.
- Behavior the user did not ask for beyond applying this same fix.

## Example

Transfers rows shrank when icon columns scrolled away (Qt remasures only visible columns). The same issue applied to Search, Share Browser, Queue, hub users, and other icon grids — those were in scope; Public Hubs (no icons) was not.
